NUM-48: apply first-order decay as exp(-K1 dt), and growth under STEADY

The node reactor (mixAtNodes) and the KINWAVE/DYNWAVE link kernel computed
c1 * (1 - k dt), copying 5.3.0's getReactedQual(), instead of
c1 * exp(-k dt) of reference manual eq. 5-6, so results depended on the
routing step. Use exp(), which also handles a negative k (growth). The
STEADY branch, which already uses exp(), skipped k < 0; apply it for any
non-zero k. Same change as NUM-48_swmm530.patch.

Unit tests that pinned the linear factor are updated: test_quality_routing
(ExecuteFirstOrderDecay), the manufactured benchmark
quality-cstr-first-order-decay (reference.csv is now 100 exp(-0.001 t), the
exact solution, instead of the recurrence 100 x 0.94^n), and
test_reaction_legacy_binding (the no-reactions parity guard now expects the
exponential, and the link double-decay bracket is re-measured: correct run
0.899 x legacy, double decay 0.150 x).

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-48_swmm600.patch

